"""FUET-5030 - 4 kHz passive electromagnetic buzzer, 5.0 x 5.0 x 3.0 mm SMD.

Datasheet: Fusheng Electronics "Specification of product" FUET-5030, drawing
FST-5030 (2018-08-28), LCSC C391031 ("BZ-DS").

Specification (BZ-DS p.2, table 1): oscillation frequency 4000 Hz with a 1/2-duty
square wave; operating voltage 2-4 Vo-p; rated voltage 3 Vo-p; current 110 mA
max at the rated voltage; sound pressure 80 dB min at 10 cm at the rated
voltage; coil resistance 12 +/- 3 ohm; -20 to +70 C operating.

Drive (BZ-DS p.4, "Recommend Driving Circuit"): + to the supply, - to a
low-side transistor driven into saturation by a 1/2-duty square wave (180 ohm
base resistor, hFE >= 200), and a diode across the coil (anode on -, cathode
on +). The switch and the diode belong to the board circuit.
Reflow (p.4): 260 C peak for 10 s max, twice at most; hand soldering 350 C
within 5 s.

Pins (BZ-DS p.2, appearance drawing): seen from the top, "+POLARITY" is the
bottom-left terminal and "-POLARITY" the bottom-right one; the bottom view shows
a third pad in the remaining corner. Footprint (LCSC/EasyEDA BUZ-SMD_FST-5030,
Altium MicrasLib): pad 1 (-1.75, +1.75) = +, pad 2 (+1.75, +1.75) = -,
pad 3 (-1.75, -1.75) = third pad. BZ-DS states no electrical function for
pad 3, so the symbol types it no_connect: it is soldered as a mechanical anchor
and left without a net.
"""

POS = io(Net)
NEG = io(Net)

Component(
    name="BUZZER",
    prefix="BZ",
    symbol=Symbol(library="FUET-5030.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("BUZ-SMD_FST-5030.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="FUET-5030", manufacturer="FUET"),
    pins={
        "+": POS,
        "-": NEG,
    },
)
